  "aboutParagraphs": [
    "Oregon Park is Atlanta's favorite beginner course — 18 gentle par 3s across 4,175 feet of open, rolling parkland with concrete tees and two permanent basket positions per hole. The silver-to-silver layout is the everyday loop, while the gold baskets stretch things out for anyone chasing more.",
    "It's free, family friendly, and the most-played course in the region for good reason: every hole gives you room to learn, and the mixed tree cover keeps things interesting without ever feeling punishing.",
    "Come for the easy round, stay for the community — this is where a huge slice of Atlanta's disc golfers took their first real putts."
  ],
