  "signatureHoleDescription": "Hole 3 is the longest at Oregon Park at 303 feet — still a par 3, still friendly, but the one hole where a big putter shot or a controlled midrange matters most. It's the perfect taste of what the course is about: accessible golf with just enough challenge to teach you something.",
  "localTips": "The silver-to-silver layout is the standard loop; the gold basket positions add distance if you want more. Free, open, and very cart friendly — a great first course. Weekends are busy, so mornings are your best bet for a quiet round.",
